o doesn't appear and didn't help? Actually contradict \"自己拍\" no. Maybe user accompanied by a friend who didn't appear? still no. Keep use \"我\" in publishing? Original trip \"我们\" but content voice \"我\" okay? User says audience knows? Fine.\n\nActually in titles \"我们\" earlier considered; we should avoid plural unknown. Use unambiguous \"我\" unless text at user statement. But their own phrase: \"我们上周末去附近山里扎营\" - \"我们\" exists reality. User says \"视频是我自己拍的，没有别人\" refers no one appears/third-party; companion presence not specified, but if companion not on camera? Hmm \"没有别人\" likely no others on camera, but actual trip \"我们\" perhaps includes another human who took photo? Wait \"视频是我自己拍的，没有别人\" means no others appeared? safe publish as \"一个人\" might be wrong if companion participated. Avoid claiming \"一个人\". Important! Do not include \"一个人\" in titles/copy except derive. We had #3 contains \"一个人\" earlier; remove because uncertain. The user says \"出镜的就我一个人\" not \"trip alone\". Use only \"出镜的只有我\". In publish copy could say \"出镜和拍摄都是我\" - user said self-shot; safe. Avoid \"一个人进山\". The original draft line \"出镜只有我\" in comments? no need. Keep no claim companion count.\nTitle candidates currently include #3 \"一个人\" - remove, replace \"没专业装备\".\nCandidate contradiction \"下雨，没专业装备，帐篷漏水——这趟还是成行了\" maybe.\nIdentity title no \"一个人\".\n\nNo claim \"没等完美天气就出发\" (subjective timing) should avoid; \"天气不好，装备普通，我们还是去了\" but plural; \"还是去了\" as subjective \"我们\"? title may say \"我们\" because trip was \"我们\" but unknown who? User's first sentence \"我们上周末去...\" implies narrator is part of \"我们\", at least user plus? They refer perhaps themselves. On camera only user; but trip could have others not appearing. Refer \"我们\" in title suggests plural party not all onscreen — could undermine single-person? Their watchers? Unknown. Better neutral title formulation without subject: \"下雨、帐篷接缝漏水，这天没白来\" overclaim. Choose leak focus: \"城边露营，帐篷接缝真的漏了水——这段我照实留了\" with \"我\" editing. Narrator \"我